{
 "_what": "COOK [the map remade, in colour] (rule 137, Paolo 10/24: 'the map still looks like shit, so we have to remake all the map assets, and let's be careful having everything look like a grey yellow sand color, I don't want that to flood all of our art'). THE DIALS of every map district picture (rule 128: the scene is kept, an era is a re-render with its own dials, never a redraw). The scene is the district factory's own geometry (tools/bohemia_district_hero_factory.py, captured by tools/bohemia_cook_the_map_capture_10_20_26.py); these dials say what colour each part of it is in ACT ONE (the ruin), and what is laid on the free ground (pools, trees, bushes, rocks). A modder edits this file. Read by tools/bohemia_cook_the_map_in_colour_10_24_26.py.",
 "era": "act1_the_ruin",
 "dust": [
